{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e"} {"question" "q-34060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\nk=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,-5⟩$, $c=⟨3,-9,15⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-2,11⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ 4s-9t=-2 \\\\ -5s+15t=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -9 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["text" "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-6⟩$, $c=⟨-2,-10,12⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,11,-12⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=2 \\\\ 7s-10t=11 \\\\ -6s+12t=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -10 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=2 \\\\ 4t=-3 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4t=-3\\,⟹\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =2 \\\\ s-2(-\\frac{3}{4}) & =2 \\\\ s+\\frac{3}{2} & =2 \\\\ s & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{1}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{1}{2}b-\\frac{3}{4}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{3}{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "411678f2d073ac452a42108f4fc348c9df8344925f88e9c45301aeb4e223ba61"} {"question" "q-74602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e"} {"question" "q-74602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake